In the coming months there will be the ability to use any number of convex bodies to form the bounds of a physics object. So as to simulate having a concave object react realistically. Like a L shaped body would have two box bounds comprise its collision bounds and it will act as if collision was precise.<br><br>These "compounds" would allow you to have your bucket, and pickup trucks, and donuts, and horseshoes ect...<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=421">Icoxo</a> — Fri May 26, 2006 11:17 pm</p><hr />
