I've started rigging up tests in anticipation of the bullet contest.  All in all, bullet is extremely great when compared to sumo and the physics simulations are awesome.<br><br> <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> But we always push for better and better things.  In sumo, there was a bounds called Polyheder.  Although it didn't function well, I miss that extra bound option.  Polyheder allowed you to make say a dynamic cup and have a ball fall into it, with all physics interactions possible.  With polyheder in bullet, it can open up more physic simulation possibilities.<br><br>Umm... if there's already an option that achieves this, I haven't seen any with the desired affects.<br><br>Jason Lin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=346">goldentaiji</a> — Fri May 26, 2006 4:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
